<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37938" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praesensĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		praesentio. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A foreboding</i>, <i>presentiment</i>
			(class.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">syn. praesagium): praesensio et scientia rerum
					futurarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 1, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedictiones et praesensiones rerum futurarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. N.
					D. 2, 3, 7</span></i>
			.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per exta inventa praesensio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Top. 20, 77</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A preconception</i>, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόληψις</span>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 17, 45</span></i>.</div>
